cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AICL in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "AICL — Architecture Compilation Language: Auditable Compilation with Proof of Origin"
abstract: >-
  AICL is a specification-first programming language in which risks,
  recoveries, and validations are mandatory syntactic elements. Every
  generated artifact carries provenance; every compilation is auditable;
  every proof of origin is cryptographically verifiable. AICL transforms
  AI best practices into mandatory structure: what is today prompt
  engineering becomes language engineering.
